Maven and Gradle are both popular build automation tools.
Maven
- A build automation and dependency management tool.
- Uses Project Object Model (POM) files written in XML.
- Focuses on convention over configuration, meaning projects follow a standard structure.
Gradle
- A modern build automation tool that supports multiple languages (Java, Kotlin, Groovy, C/C++).

⚖️ Comparison Table
Feature	        Maven	            Gradle
Configuration	XML (POM file)	    Groovy/Kotlin DSL
Performance	    Slower builds	    Faster builds (incremental + caching)
Flexibility	    convention-driven	Highly customizable
Ecosystem	    Mature, widely      Growing, dominant in Android projects
                used in enterprises	


📌 Spring Initializer Context
When you use Spring Initializer to bootstrap a Spring Boot project, you can choose either Maven or Gradle:

Maven is often chosen for enterprise projects where stability and convention are valued.

Gradle is preferred when you want faster builds, flexibility, or if you’re working with Android.

 the choice depends on your team’s preference and project requirements.


